\subsection{Definitions and mathematical statement}
\paragraph{Statement recorded in the supplied source.}
For every fixed positive half-integer spin S in the nearest-neighbor $Z^3$ quantum Heisenberg ferromagnet, does (beta $S)^{5/2}[S-m_S(\beta )-n_S^sw(\beta )]\to 0$ as beta$\to$infinity, where $n_S^sw$ is the full lattice spin-wave Bose occupation integral?

\subsection{Short English statement}
For every fixed positive half-integer spin S in the nearest-neighbor $Z^3$ quantum Heisenberg ferromagnet, does (beta $S)^{5/2}[S-m_S(\beta )-n_S^sw(\beta )]\to 0$ as beta$\to$infinity, where $n_S^sw$ is the full lattice spin-wave Bose occupation integral?

\subsection{Sources}
\begin{itemize}
\item[S1] Original question source or mathematical context.
\url{https://github.com/openai/math/blob/adc7f1241b42e322a6451854ab7e4b4c146bf78a/preprints/The-first-lattice-correction-to-Blochs-law-October-5-2026/build/sections/01-introduction.tex}.
